---
const siteUrl = 'https://1000namesofmakali.com';
const canonical = `${siteUrl}/about/`;
const title = 'About the Project & Author | Adya Mahakali 1000 Names';
const description =
	'About the Adya Mahakali 1000 Names project: the author, the source basis, the transliteration approach, and how corrections are handled.';

const schema = {
	'@context': 'https://schema.org',
	'@graph': [
		{
			'@type': 'ProfilePage',
			'@id': `${canonical}#webpage`,
			name: title,
			description,
			url: canonical,
			inLanguage: 'en',
			isPartOf: { '@id': `${siteUrl}/#website` },
			mainEntity: { '@id': `${siteUrl}/#publisher` },
		},
		{
			'@type': 'Person',
			'@id': `${siteUrl}/#publisher`,
			name: 'Kaliputra Ashish',
			description:
				'Author and maintainer of the Adya Mahakali 1000 Names project, a free devotional reference for the Adya Mahakali Sahasranama.',
			url: canonical,
			sameAs: [
				'https://github.com/09ashishkapoor',
				'https://www.instagram.com/ashishkaliputra',
				'https://archive.org/details/adya-mahakali-sahasranama-kaliputraashish',
			],
			knowsAbout: ['Adya Mahakali Sahasranama', 'Kali Sahasranama', 'Shakta devotional literature'],
		},
		{
			'@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
			'@id': `${canonical}#breadcrumb`,
			itemListElement: [
				{ '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: `${siteUrl}/` },
				{ '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'About', item: canonical },
			],
		},
	],
};
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="UTF-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
		<title>{title}</title>
		<meta name="description" content={description} />
		<meta name="robots" content="index,follow,max-image-preview:large,max-snippet:-1" />
		<meta property="og:type" content="article" />
		<meta property="og:title" content={title} />
		<meta property="og:description" content={description} />
		<meta property="og:url" content={canonical} />
		<meta property="og:image" content="https://1000namesofmakali.com/MaaAdyaKali_5.webp" />
		<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
		<meta name="twitter:title" content={title} />
		<meta name="twitter:description" content={description} />
		<meta name="twitter:image" content="https://1000namesofmakali.com/MaaAdyaKali_5.webp" />
		<link rel="canonical" href={canonical} />
		<link rel="alternate" type="text/plain" href="/llms.txt" title="LLMs text summary" />
		<link rel="stylesheet" href="/static-pages.css" />
		<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)}></script>
	</head>
	<body class="names-static names-static--about">
		<main>
			<nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
				<ol>
					<li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
					<li><span aria-current="page">About</span></li>
				</ol>
			</nav>

			<p class="page-kicker">About the project</p>
			<h1>About Adya Mahakali 1000 Names</h1>

			<figure class="page-figure">
				<img
					src="/MaaAdyaKali_5.webp"
					alt="Statue of Maa Adya Mahakali with a trident, skull garland, and red hibiscus flowers"
					width="1920"
					height="1080"
					loading="lazy"
					decoding="async"
				/>
				<figcaption>Maa Adya Mahakali — devotional image used on this site.</figcaption>
			</figure>

			<section class="hero-panel">
				<p class="intro">
					<strong>Adya Mahakali 1000 Names</strong> is a free devotional reference for the Adya Mahakali
					Sahasranama: 1,072 names of Maa Adya Mahakali with English meanings, Devanagari spellings, and
					transliteration. It is maintained by <strong>Kaliputra Ashish</strong> and dedicated to
					<strong>Shri Praveen Radhakrishnan</strong> and the <strong>Khyapa Parampara</strong>.
				</p>
				<nav class="page-nav" aria-label="About navigation">
					<ul>
						<li><a href="/names/">Browse all names</a></li>
						<li><a href="/kali-sahasranama-pdf/">Free PDF editions</a></li>
						<li><a href="/sources/">Sources and editorial method</a></li>
						<li><a href="/contact/">Contact and corrections</a></li>
					</ul>
				</nav>
			</section>

			<section class="source-notes">
				<h2>What this site is</h2>
				<p>
					The project exists to support devotional reading and study of the Maa Adya Mahakali Sahasranama. It
					presents the full name list with one-line meanings and longer explanatory notes, a searchable reader, a
					static names hub, and printable PDF editions. Everything is offered free, without registration.
				</p>
				<p>
					The site is intentionally simple and open: it is a static website with no accounts and no paywall, and its
					source code is public.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="source-notes">
				<h2>How the text was compiled</h2>
				<p>
					The names follow the Adya Mahakali Sahasranama as compiled for this project. Public reference material and
					the broader Shakta devotional tradition informed the explanatory notes. The English meanings and
					elaborations are interpretive study notes, not a translation of a single critical edition.
				</p>
				<p>
					The source basis, editorial approach, and citation guidance are documented on the
					<a href="/sources/">sources page</a>.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="source-notes">
				<h2>Transliteration approach</h2>
				<p>
					Sanskrit names reach English readers in several romanizations. Each name page shows a common English
					spelling, the IAST form, the Devanagari form, and the source transliteration used by this project. The
					mapping is generated from the site's data, so corrections are made once and applied across every page.
				</p>
				<p>
					If a spelling matters for your practice or citation, use the IAST or Devanagari form on the individual
					name page as the reference.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="source-notes">
				<h2>Open source and corrections</h2>
				<p>
					The site is open source. Spelling, meaning, formatting, attribution, and source issues can be reported
					through the public repository, which keeps the correction reviewable. See the
					<a href="/contact/">contact page</a> for the best ways to reach the maintainer.
				</p>
				<p>
					<a href="https://github.com/09ashishkapoor/1000namesofmaadya" rel="noopener noreferrer">View the project repository</a>
				</p>
			</section>
		</main>
	</body>
</html>
